# ---------------------------------------------------------------- ignored
# Environments and build output. All of this is regenerated by setup and by
# running the code, so it must never enter the repository.
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.nbi
*.nbc
.pytest_cache/

# The raw shard tree is ~2,400 files and 31 MB. It is published as the single
# archive results/shards.tar.gz instead, which is 3.9 MB. Build it with:
#     tar -czf results/shards.tar.gz results/shards
results/shards/
results/*.csv

# Word working documents and their generators (delete these four lines if you
# decide to publish the manuscript alongside the code).
Findings.docx
RQ5_Findings.docx
make_findings.js

# Private working notes: run order, state of the study, outstanding tasks.
# Kept locally, not published.
NOTES.md

# Scratch
Claude outputs/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- tracked
# Listed here only as a reminder. These are NOT ignored, and the paper's
# Data and Code Availability statement promises every one of them:
#
#   colreg/                    the package
#   scripts/                   runners, analyses, audits, figures
#   tests/                     parity suite against scikit-learn
#   data/corpus_manifest.json  how each dataset was resolved and characterised
#   data/excluded_datasets.json
#   data/cache/*.npz           the 24 resolved design matrices (9 MB)
#   results/figures/*.png      the published figures
#   results/stability.json     selection stability results
#   results/shards.tar.gz      the fold-level results (3.9 MB)
#   README.md, requirements.txt, pyproject.toml, VERSION
#   setup.bat, setup.ps1, SETUP_WINDOWS.md
